# Slices

A slice is a dynamically sized view into an underlying container. Unlike arrays, which have a strict, fixed length, slices can grow and shrink. In GX, slices are often used to store the axis lengths of arrays (see next lesson).

A slice is specified using the `[]` prefix without a size. In this example, the function `Main` returns an array (type `[2]int64`), a slice (type `[]int64`), and a slice of slices (type `[][]int64`).

Like arrays with several axes, slices can contain other slices. Unlike arrays, a slice can contain slices of different lengths, like the last value returned by `Main`.

For Python developers, arrays and slices in GX are respectively equivalent to NumPy arrays and Python lists.

